{{also|TIL|'til|тіл}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|til}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|til||to, until}}, possibly from {{etyl|non|-}} {{m|non|til}}, both from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*tila-||goal}}, or {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*til||to, towards}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*ád||near, at}}. Compare to {{etyl|ofs|-}} {{term|til|lang=ofs}}
<!--note that the OED says it is RELATED to the Old Norse til rather than derived from it. http://oxforddictionaries.com/definition/till-->

